</section>
<section aria-labelledby="tone-h">
  <h2 id="tone-h" class="type-h2">Tones</h2>
  <p>The plain tone sits on <code>surface/neutral/base</code>. The tint tone sits on <code>surface/brand/primary/subtle</code>. The tint marks the sections that carry the argument of the page, such as the problem and the outcome.</p>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="layout-h">
  <h2 id="layout-h" class="type-h2">Layout and spacing</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Section split layout by breakpoint, scrollable">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Breakpoint</th><th scope="col">Layout</th><th scope="col">Padding above and below</th><th scope="col">Gap between parts</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">Mobile</th><td>Label, statement and body stacked, 4 columns</td><td>48px</td><td>48px</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Tablet (768px up)</th><td>8 columns. The label takes the full width. The body starts at column 3.</td><td>64px</td><td>48px</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Desktop (1024px up)</th><td>12 columns. The label takes columns 1 to 8 and the body columns 9 to 12.</td><td>80px</td><td>64px</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>The label and the statement are 16px apart. The side padding is the page padding. The section keeps 64px of scroll margin so a jump link does not park it under the header. Images follow the text in a gallery inside the same section.</p>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="color-h">
  <h2 id="color-h" class="type-h2">Color</h2>
  <p>The section name is <code>text/brand/primary</code>. The statement is <code>text/neutral/primary</code>. The body is <code>text/neutral/body</code>.</p>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="use-h">
  <h2 id="use-h" class="type-h2">Using the section split</h2>
  <div class="rules">
    <div class="rule"><h3 class="type-h3">Do</h3><ul>
      <li>Make the statement one sentence that someone could read alone and get the point.</li>
      <li>Give the section an <code>id</code> so the jump nav can point to it.</li>
    </ul></div>
    <div class="rule"><h3 class="type-h3">Don't</h3><ul>
      <li>Use red or yellow for the section name. Brand blue is the only name color.</li>
      <li>Make the two sides an even 50/50.</li>
    </ul></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="a11y-h">
  <h2 id="a11y-h" class="type-h2">Accessibility</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The section is a <code>&lt;section&gt;</code> named by its heading (<code>aria-labelledby</code>).</li>
    <li>The section name is a real <code>h2</code> on a case study page, so the sections show in a screen reader's heading list. The demos here use <code>h3</code> because the docs page already has an <code>h2</code>.</li>
    <li>The text is body copy with <code>text-wrap: pretty</code>, so a paragraph does not end on a single word.</li>
  </ul>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="html-h">
  <h2 id="html-h" class="type-h2">The HTML</h2>
